  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Venture capitalist Todd Chaffee developed Cierto Tequila after researching the use of artificial additives in spirits. He partnered with Mexican distillers Enrique Fonseca and Sergio Mendoza, whose agave-growing experience and reserves of aged tequila provided the production foundation. The team tested blends with consumers and entered competitions before offering the brand publicly.\n\nA video of two brothers distributing blankets prompted another commitment. Chaffee offered Nick and Mike Fio financial support and mentoring to develop Blankets of Hope, encouraging them to concentrate on the project. Its school workshops invite pupils to write personal messages that accompany blankets delivered to people experiencing homelessness.",
    "html": "<p>Venture capitalist Todd Chaffee developed Cierto Tequila after researching the use of artificial additives in spirits. He partnered with Mexican distillers Enrique Fonseca and Sergio Mendoza, whose agave-growing experience and reserves of aged tequila provided the production foundation. The team tested blends with consumers and entered competitions before offering the brand publicly.</p>\r\n<p>A video of two brothers distributing blankets prompted another commitment. Chaffee offered Nick and Mike Fio financial support and mentoring to develop Blankets of Hope, encouraging them to concentrate on the project. Its school workshops invite pupils to write personal messages that accompany blankets delivered to people experiencing homelessness.</p>\r\n",
    "word_count": 101,
